# 🔄 DEX Audit Checklist

## Swap Functions

- [ ] Slippage protection enforced (minAmountOut parameter)
- [ ] Deadline parameter checked against block.timestamp
- [ ] Proper handling of fee-on-transfer tokens
- [ ] K constant/invariant verified after swap
- [ ] No reentrancy during swap execution
- [ ] Price impact limits enforced
- [ ] Flash swap repayment verified

## Liquidity Management

- [ ] First depositor attack mitigated (minimum liquidity / dead shares)
- [ ] LP tokens minted proportionally to contribution
- [ ] Remove liquidity reentrancy protected
- [ ] Proportional asset withdrawal ensured
- [ ] Minimum deposit amounts enforced
- [ ] Donation attacks prevented

## Price Oracles

- [ ] TWAP implementation uses sufficient window (>30 min)
- [ ] Cumulative price overflow handled
- [ ] Oracle manipulation resistance verified
- [ ] Stale price protection implemented
- [ ] Multiple oracle sources compared when possible

## Fee Handling

- [ ] Fee calculation doesn't overflow
- [ ] Fee parameters bounded to reasonable range
- [ ] Fee changes timelocked or capped
- [ ] Protocol fee collection doesn't break invariants
- [ ] LP fee distribution accurate

## Pool Creation

- [ ] Pool creation permissioned or has fees to prevent spam
- [ ] Initial price validation (reasonable bounds)
- [ ] Token pair validation (no identical tokens)
- [ ] Pool address deterministically calculable
- [ ] Factory ownership properly managed

## Token Compatibility

### Standard ERC20
- [ ] Return value checked on transfer/approve
- [ ] Balance changes correctly calculated

### Fee-on-Transfer
- [ ] Actual received amount calculated via balance diff
- [ ] Fee doesn't break invariants

### Rebasing
- [ ] Balance changes between transactions handled
- [ ] Interest accrual doesn't break accounting

### Low Decimals (e.g., USDC)
- [ ] Precision loss acceptable
- [ ] Rounding direction correct

### High Decimals
- [ ] No overflow in calculations
- [ ] Precision maintained

### Blacklist Tokens (USDC/USDT)
- [ ] Blacklisted transfers don't block other users
- [ ] Emergency handling for blacklisted pools

### ERC777
- [ ] Hooks don't enable reentrancy
- [ ] Or ERC777 tokens explicitly not supported

## Access Control

- [ ] Admin functions properly protected
- [ ] Parameter changes bounded
- [ ] Emergency pause mechanism
- [ ] Pause doesn't trap user funds
- [ ] Upgrade mechanism secure

## Concentrated Liquidity (Uniswap V3 style)

- [ ] Tick math correct
- [ ] Price range boundaries valid
- [ ] Position accounting accurate
- [ ] Tick crossing handled correctly
- [ ] Fee accumulation per tick correct
- [ ] Active liquidity calculation accurate

## Uniswap V4 Hooks

- [ ] Hook permissions correctly declared
- [ ] Hooks cannot manipulate pool unfairly
- [ ] Hook reentrancy safe
- [ ] Hook return values validated
- [ ] Flash accounting correct with hooks

## Multi-Hop Swaps

- [ ] Intermediate tokens don't accumulate
- [ ] Path validation (no loops)
- [ ] Gas limits considered for long paths
- [ ] Slippage applied to final output

## Flash Loans/Swaps

- [ ] Callback validation correct
- [ ] Repayment verified atomically
- [ ] Flash fee calculation correct
- [ ] Can't be used to manipulate pool state unfairly

## Cross-Pool Operations

- [ ] Arbitrage doesn't drain pools unfairly
- [ ] No flash loan attacks across pools
- [ ] Price consistency across related pools

## Gas Optimization Security

- [ ] Gas optimizations don't introduce bugs
- [ ] Unchecked blocks properly bounded
- [ ] Assembly operations correct

## Testing Coverage

- [ ] Fuzz testing for swap functions
- [ ] Invariant testing for K constant
- [ ] Edge cases tested (0 amounts, max amounts)
- [ ] Economic attacks simulated
